I've had success skeletonizing and 3d plotting my nrrd files as dotprops objects, but I've run into issues trying to achieve the following:

1) visualizing the intersect of multiple GAL4 expression patterns in 3D space, superimposed on a surface plot of the ventral nervous system standard

2) determining whether any of these intersections can be assigned to distinct tracts or commissures in the VNS

This seemed pretty straightforward at first but with one complication: I am not generating single-cell clones, so the dotprops objects will represent multiple neurons. Additionally, raster 3d objects (like im3ds) seem like a better choice for generating the sort of '3d heatmaps' I'd like to get, but as far as I can tell the intersect functions can only handle vector objects. Any advice?

