The pruning function works perfectly; by successively pruning my largest expression pattern with the next largest and so on, within a loop that does this for smaller and smaller maxdist values, I can generate a decent heatmap. The only issue I run into now is that plot3d doesn't seem to support transparency for dotprops objects: when I set the alpha to anything but 1.0 the image doesn't show up in the RGL device at all. Is there a workaround for this?

As for the tracts, I know that Boerner and Duch (2010) registered the known tracts and commissures to a vns standard, but I have yet to ask them for the files, if they are available at all. We have a PC with Amira here so as a last resort we can do the anatomical registration by hand.

